59,3,,status,Daisuke,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Victoria,,Option A is fixed desks. Option B is rotating blocks. Option C is free address.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Minato,,Option A sounds best for my back. I can set it up once.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,May,,"Option C is risky. If I arrive late, I get a bad desk.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,Option B is expensive. We pay the facilities fee every rotation.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,Option A might isolate us if we're not careful with grouping.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Shunichi, you're right about the cost of B. 6,200 yen per desk per move.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Minato,,"@May, with C, you might get the loud printer row. That's bad.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,May,,"@Minato, true. But with A, I need to know I get a good spot.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Daisuke, if we group by function in A, we might lose cross-talk.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I think A is safest, but we need to ensure we can still collaborate.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Victoria,,The billing data suggests we should minimize empty space. A does that.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Minato,,I agree. A is the most comfortable for me.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,May,,"I'm leaning towards A, but I want to make sure the morning isn't chaotic.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,A allows us to assign the window seats deliberately. That addresses the survey.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,"If we assign seats by function, we might sit with similar people. Is that okay?","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Victoria,,We can mitigate that by mixing functions slightly in the grouping.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Minato,,"That sounds good. I just want a quiet, comfortable spot.","{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,May,,I'll accept A if the setup is quick. The badge data shows varied arrivals.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,A is the most rational choice. It minimizes cost and maximizes comfort.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,I'll go with A. I trust we can manage the social side.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
